<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="054" project="spaarkeai-compose-r8">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-C03 (whole-document half) — enumerate the closed paraId set for the whole-document review pass and deliver it to the model; catalog change for `compose-revise-document`</title>
    <phase>5 Track C — AI Edit Placement</phase>
    <gate>blocked-on-051</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes what the whole-document review pass sends to the model and what its Action contract requires back; may cross into the SpaarkeAi code page (a hot path).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Capability-matched: the judgment is WHERE the closed set is enumerated — server-side from `ChatSession.ReferenceMap`, or client-side across a pane boundary — and both candidate homes sit near lines the project has already fenced (C-7's admission-gate boundary; ADR-043's "no engine reads hardcoded session state"). Choosing wrong here either re-opens a governance line or ships a second supply mechanism that task 055 then has to consume. Implementing either half, once chosen, is not the hard part.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Same Compose edit spine as 051/052/053; may also touch `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/**`.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>051</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, frontend, compose, ai, spaarke-ai, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Task 051 gave the SELECTION-scoped Compose capabilities a deterministic anchor end to end: the client
    captures a `w14:paraId`, ADR-043 Amendment 1 carries it into the model's `## Input`, the Action schema
    lets the model echo it back, and `ComposeAnchorResolver` places by it with zero text matching.

    The WHOLE-DOCUMENT review pass (`compose-revise-document`) is the one path that still cannot work that
    way, for a real reason: there is no selection, so there is no single paraId to send. It needs the other
    half of FR-C03 — an ENUMERATED CLOSED SET of the document's paragraphs, supplied to the model, with the
    model required to return an id drawn from that set.

    The validate half already exists and is tested (`ComposeAnchorResolver` membership check →
    `EditErrorKind.UnknownParaId`, refused loudly, never guessed). This task owns the SUPPLY half.

    **The decision this task exists to make.** Where is the set enumerated?

      (a) SERVER-SIDE from `ChatSession.ReferenceMap` (built at Compose Load, already persisted, already
          the authoritative map `CitationResolver` reads). The dispatch already carries
          `documentSessionId`, so the server can resolve it with NO client change and NO cross-pane
          hand-off. Tension to resolve honestly: ADR-043's "no engine reads hardcoded session state", and
          C-7's "not as a new admission gate in `SessionDispatchOrchestrator`". Neither obviously forbids
          resolving a DECLARED input from session state — that is arguably the binder's own job — but the
          line must be argued, not assumed.

      (b) CLIENT-SIDE in `ConversationPane.tsx` (SpaarkeAi), which builds the dispatch slots today but does
          NOT hold the paraId map — that lives in the Compose pane. Requires a cross-pane hand-off, makes
          SpaarkeAi a hot-path touch, and lets a client assert the closed set the server will validate
          against, which is the weaker trust position.

    Pick one, state why in the task notes, and cite ADR-043 Amendment 1 (the companion-input channel this
    rides on — no new mechanism is owed). If the chosen path needs SpaarkeAi changes, make them HERE; there
    is no hand-off to another project.

    **Then the catalog change, and NOT before the supply exists.** `compose-revise-document`'s `edits[]` and
    `comments[]` gain `target_para_id`; its `sprk_inputschema` declares the paragraph-set input; the
    systemPrompt gains the same TARGET IDENTITY rule the three selection Actions carry. Landing the schema
    first would ask the model for ids it was never given and refuse every whole-document edit — strictly
    worse than today's prose matching. Supply and catalog land together.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer. Expert in the Compose projection/reference map, `ContextBinder`'s declared-input channel (ADR-043 Amendment 1), the SpaarkeAi ConversationPane dispatch, and the Compose catalog Action seeds.</role>

  <goal>
    The whole-document review pass supplies the model an enumerated closed set of the document's paragraphs,
    and `compose-revise-document` requires an id drawn from that set. An id outside it is refused loudly.
    No second supply mechanism is introduced — the set rides the ADR-043 Amendment 1 declared-input channel.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      ADR-043 Amendment 1 (task 051, §6.5 Path B) opened the channel this task needs: an Action's DECLARED
      inputs render into `## Input` alongside the operand. The paragraph set is just another declared input —
      that is why the amendment was written generically rather than as a paraId special case.

      Task 051 also proved the failure mode to avoid: a consumer built before its producer. Three links were
      dark in one session (the Action schema, the Action `inputSchema`, and the deploy script's
      `sprk_inputschema` mapping). Verify each link of THIS chain by test before declaring it done.

      Size matters here in a way it did not for a single paraId. A whole document's paragraph set is many
      entries; `ContextBinder`'s companion cap (`MaxDeclaredCompanionChars`) SKIPS an oversized value and
      logs rather than truncating, precisely so a half-sent set is never presented to the model as complete.
      Measure a realistic worst case and decide deliberately: trim the set (headings + numbered clauses
      only?), raise the cap, or page it. Do NOT let it silently hit the cap.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="primary-edit">infra/dataverse/actions/compose-revise-document.action.json</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/ContextBinder.cs</file>
      <file role="primary-edit">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeAnchorResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Compose/ComposeService.cs (BuildReferenceMap)</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Models/Ai/Chat/ChatSession.cs (ReferenceMap)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md (Amendment 1)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/adr-043-041-assessment.md (C-1 as amended, C-4, C-7)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-043 Amendment 1">The set MUST ride the DECLARED-input channel. MUST NOT add a fourth `OperandVocabulary` entry (pick-one list — it would displace `selectionText`), and MUST NOT nest it inside the operand value (type pun).</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 050 C-7">MUST NOT add a new admission gate in `SessionDispatchOrchestrator`, and MUST NOT add a new dispatch protocol, catalog kind, or `ActionKind`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project invariant 3">The projection is the ONLY coordinate system. The closed set MUST be the projection/session reference map — never a second enumeration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Catalog change and supply MUST land together. Requiring `target_para_id` before the set is supplied refuses every whole-document edit — worse than today.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 050 C-4">ADR-040 caps inline payloads at 128 KB and `ChatEndpoints.ProjectComposeOutputs` SKIPS truncated entries. A whole-document change list that now carries an anchor per edit grows. Measure the worst case and report headroom or the degradation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §17">If SpaarkeAi is touched, run `/conflict-check` FIRST, update the `projects/INDEX.md` hot-path row, and deploy BFF + `sprk_spaarkeai` together (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT delete or retire anything. Task 052 owns retirement and MUST NOT run until this task and 055 land.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Seam tests. Every link verified by a test that was observed to FAIL before its fix — no consumer built for an unverified producer.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Declared-input channel, session reference map, whole-document review dispatch</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-049-compose-shadow-document.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/adr-043-041-assessment.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/spec.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor declaration">Declare rigor FULL; load the ADR-043 amendment and the assessment (C-1 as amended, C-4, C-7) FIRST.</step>
    <step order="1">Trace the whole-document dispatch end to end and record where the paragraph set could enter. Name every link, as task 051 had to.</step>
    <step order="2">DECIDE server-side vs client-side enumeration. Write the reasoning + the ADR line you are arguing against or within into `notes/`. Escalate per §6.5 if it needs an amendment.</step>
    <step order="3">Size the set on a real corpus document. Decide trim / raise-cap / page BEFORE implementing, and never let it silently hit the companion cap.</step>
    <step order="4">Write the failing seam test for the supply link, observe it fail, then implement.</step>
    <step order="5">Land the `compose-revise-document` catalog change (inputSchema + `edits[]`/`comments[]` `target_para_id` + TARGET IDENTITY prompt rule) in the SAME change as the supply.</step>
    <step order="6">Flip the negative test in `ComposeEditActionAnchorContractSeamTests` that currently PINS the whole-document omission, and move the Action onto the anchored list.</step>
    <step order="7">Publish-size + no-new-NuGet + no-new-HIGH-CVE report; `/conflict-check` if SpaarkeAi was touched.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If server-side enumeration cannot be reconciled with ADR-043's "no engine reads hardcoded session state" without straining it, surface the conflict per §6.5 rather than choosing the client path by default to avoid the argument — the trust position matters more than the convenience.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the realistic paragraph set cannot fit the companion cap without trimming that would make the closed set incomplete, STOP: an incomplete "closed" set is a contradiction, and the model would be refused on ids that genuinely exist.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">infra/dataverse/actions/compose-revise-document.action.json</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Context/ContextBinder.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx (if the client path is chosen)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Compose/</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r8/notes/054-closed-set-supply-decision.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A whole-document review dispatch supplies the model an enumerated closed set of the document's paragraphs, asserted by a seam test that reads the RENDERED prompt.</criterion>
    <criterion>The set is the projection/session reference map — no second enumeration exists (verified by reading).</criterion>
    <criterion>`compose-revise-document` declares the set as an input AND requires `target_para_id` on `edits[]` and `comments[]`.</criterion>
    <criterion>A returned id outside the set is refused loudly and never guessed (already implemented; asserted here for the whole-document path).</criterion>
    <criterion>The enumeration decision is documented with its reasoning and the ADR line it was argued against.</criterion>
    <criterion>Worst-case set size measured on a real corpus document; headroom stated, or the degradation stated explicitly. The companion cap is never hit silently.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every link verified by a test observed to FAIL before its fix.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: no fourth `OperandVocabulary` entry; the operand is not displaced.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: no new dispatch, catalog kind, or `ActionKind`; no new admission gate in `SessionDispatchOrchestrator`.</criterion>
    <criterion>NEGATIVE: nothing deleted or retired.</criterion>
    <criterion>If SpaarkeAi was touched: `/conflict-check` run, `projects/INDEX.md` updated, co-deploy noted.</criterion>
    <criterion>Publish size reported; no new NuGet; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
